@design/sigil-wiring.sigil from SigilWiring import {
  experiment arm, evaluator subagent, interpreter agent, answer file, sigil repository,
}
@design/task-core.sigil from TaskCore import {
  session usage, transcript, launch spec,
}
@design/agent-config.sigil from AgentConfig import { thinking level }
@design/claude-mcp-server.sigil from ClaudeMcpServer import { allow rule }
@design/task-store.sigil from TaskStore import { task record }

component SpikeHarness {
  goal {
    Run an experiment arm on a fresh copy of the planted Slotted design, score
    it,
    and write one row of measures, so that a person can decide from a table
    whether
    delegating interpreters to a local model is good enough.
  }

  state {
    A *pass directory* is the Claude working directory of one run. It holds
    root,
    the fixture copy, store, an empty private *claims store*, run, skills, the
    *staged sigil skills*, and .agents/subzero.yaml.

    A *planted problem* is one of the four known faults in the planted Slotted
    design. A *measurement row* holds the outcome of each planted problem, the
    final ingest state, the re-asks used, the units left unread, the token
    usage
    split into main conversation, evaluator subagent and interpreters, the wall
    time and the context use at settle of the interpreters. It also holds the
    thinking level that the launch spec of each pi interpreter declares, and
    the
    stray writes of each interpreter, which are its writes outside its
    answer file.
    The *spike results document* is docs/spike-results.md.
  }

  logic {
    Stage a fresh pass directory from the planted fixture with no claims store.
    Run
    the experiment arm with claude -p from the pass directory. Run sigilc check
    on
    the pass directory itself and score each planted problem from that report
    against the answer key. Read usage from the stream, the transcript of each
    subagent
    and, for the interpreter agent on pi, the session usage in the task record.
    List the files that the write calls of each interpreter name in its own
    transcript or pi session, and compare each with the answer file of its
    brief.
    Append a measurement row to the table. The flow ends when the row is
    appended,
    and a run without an evaluator report is appended as failed.
  }

  constraints {
    The sigil repository must stay read-only. The harness may import its
    fixture,
    preflight, design view and evidence validation by path, and must
    re-implement
    the *issue matcher* that scores each planted problem without changing it.

    The score of each planted problem must come from the sigilc check the
    harness
    runs itself, so that it reflects what the interpreters read and not whether
    a
    write-back succeeded.

    A run in a pass directory must use dontAsk with an explicit allow-list, so
    that
    an unlisted tool is denied and never prompted. SpikeHarness provides the
    allow rule for the subzero tools in the allow-list of each experiment arm
    that
    uses delegation. It must not use --no-session-persistence, because that
    suppresses the transcript of each subagent, and not --strict-mcp-config,
    because
    that
    drops the plugin's MCP server in B.

    An *anchor Facet* that was not read must score its planted problem as N/A
    and
    not as missed. A finding with the right class and law but the wrong subject
    must count as extra and not as a match. A *cumulative token counter* must
    be
    counted once and not once per event.

    A run that ends without the evaluator's report must be kept as a failed
    measurement row and never dropped.

    The writes of each interpreter must be read from its own transcript, with
    every
    path normalized against the pass directory. A pass with a write other than
    the
    answer file must be kept and flagged, never failed or dropped, and a write
    into
    the claims store of the pass directory must be called out as making the
    score
    untrustworthy.

    The measurement row must record the thinking level that the launch spec
    declares, and not the level that the server applied. A field that the
    session usage marks unavailable must stay unavailable in the row with its
    reason, and must never become zero.

    The harness must run each experiment arm on the same *design revision* and
    the
    same Claude model and effort. The comparison is three matched passes each
    of A
    and B, plus one B-low pass, one A-cheap pass and one B-control pass.

    No threshold applies. The decision of whether to build the next version is
    written by the user in the spike results document, citing the table.
  }

  cases {
    Scoring the stored workspace of an existing sigil benchmark run gives the
    same
    outcome for each planted problem as that run's own report.

    A measurement row built from a stream with a transcript from each of two
    subagents splits
    the
    usage per subagent.

    A pass in which an interpreter writes a second file is kept and flagged,
    and
    its measurement row shows the path.
  }

  interface {
    Run one experiment arm on a fresh pass directory with its
    staged sigil skills,
    and append one measurement row, with every measure filled or marked
    unavailable
    with a reason.

    Produce a table with one measurement row per pass, keeping each failed
    pass.

    Provide the spike results document with the table, the plumbing checks of
    the
    delegation requirements with evidence pointers, and a place for the
    decision
    that the user writes.
  }

  decisions {
    The harness is Deno because it imports the sigil benchmark's own Deno
    TypeScript by path. The review quality of the evaluator subagent stays a
    manual
    record. The writes of an interpreter are detected from its transcript and
    not
    from a before and after listing, because the evaluator writes many files in
    the
    same directory at the same time. The context use is named at settle because
    the
    session usage reports the value at the end of the run and not its peak.
  }
}
